  "metadata": {
    "title": "Coordinated Online Targeting and Doxxing of Women",
    "data_classification": "Synthetic / fictional",
    "purpose": "Second demonstration case. Exercises capabilities the stalking case does not: multi-victim aggregation, entity resolution across anonymous social handles, digital-infrastructure and payment trails, and cross-case repeat-pattern linkage.",
    "provenance": "Entirely fictional. Every person, handle, number, payment reference and domain below is invented for testing. No real individual, platform, investigation or case is represented, and nothing here is derived from any real reported matter.",
    "why_this_pattern": "App- and web-based coordinated targeting of women is a recognised category of cyber-harassment in India. This case models the general structure of that offence category - anonymous operator accounts, shared hosting infrastructure, a payment trail, and multiple complainants filing separately - so the platform can be tested against a multi-victim digital case rather than a single-victim physical one."
  },
